<title>USA: Baldwin Piano says to cut workforce.</title>
<headline>Baldwin Piano says to cut workforce.</headline>
<dateline>LOVELAND, Ohio 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baldwin Piano &amp; Organ Co said on Tuesday that it is cutting its workforce by about 15 percent in order to reduce overheads and improve competitiveness.</p>
<p>The company said the reduction in workforce represents about 50 salaried positions at four locations:  the headquarters in Loveland, Ohio, and the manufacturing plants at Greenwood in Mississippi, Trumann in Arkansas, and Fayetteville, also in Arkansas.</p>
<p>&quot;Due to the loss of contract manufacturing for two piano companies earlier in the year, we must get our overhead costs in line with revenues,&quot; president and chief executive Karen Hendricks said in a statement.</p>
</text>
